WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.306 --> 00:00:03.125
- Hello everyone, this
is Evan, this is Nina.

00:00:03.125 --> 00:00:05.606
- Wow. What's up, Believe Nation?

00:00:05.606 --> 00:00:08.145
Nina and I are heading
on a vacation to London

00:00:08.145 --> 00:00:10.700
and then hopping a cruise across Europe.

00:00:10.700 --> 00:00:13.927
And you guys are joining us on our trip.

00:00:13.927 --> 00:00:16.510
(upbeat music)

00:00:27.783 --> 00:00:28.873
So Nina and I haven't,

00:00:28.873 --> 00:00:29.945
when was the last time
we went on vacation?

00:00:29.945 --> 00:00:31.674
- Two Summers. Just us?

00:00:31.674 --> 00:00:32.507
- Yeah.

00:00:32.507 --> 00:00:35.451
- I don't remember. No,
we didn't go last year.

00:00:35.451 --> 00:00:37.931
We went the year before. We went to

00:00:37.931 --> 00:00:39.186
- Asia?

00:00:39.186 --> 00:00:42.544
- No, not Asia. Oh yes,
that was the Asia trip.

00:00:42.544 --> 00:00:44.219
- I've traveled too much this year.

00:00:44.219 --> 00:00:46.497
I've had six trips already,
I think, this year.

00:00:46.497 --> 00:00:49.327
It's too much. I don't like getting out.

00:00:49.327 --> 00:00:51.235
I got a lot of work to do.

00:00:51.235 --> 00:00:53.031
But, we decided we're going to go.

00:00:53.031 --> 00:00:54.812
Nina has never been to London.

00:00:54.812 --> 00:00:55.846
- Yes.

00:00:55.846 --> 00:00:58.324
- So she's excited. I'm
going to show her around.

00:00:58.324 --> 00:00:59.464
And then we're going to hop a cruise

00:00:59.464 --> 00:01:01.881
and go to some new countries.

00:01:03.092 --> 00:01:04.930
Meet up some friends,
discover some new things,

00:01:04.930 --> 00:01:06.847
eat a lot of bad food.

00:01:07.823 --> 00:01:09.408
- Nina's already started
her crappy diet today.

00:01:09.408 --> 00:01:10.241
- Yummy food.

00:01:10.241 --> 00:01:11.832
- Oh yeah, yummy food, but bad for you.

00:01:11.832 --> 00:01:12.665
- Yeah.

00:01:12.665 --> 00:01:13.744
- And we're waiting for our Uber

00:01:13.744 --> 00:01:14.610
so we can hop to the airport.

00:01:14.610 --> 00:01:17.193
(upbeat music)

00:01:32.630 --> 00:01:34.880
Nina's getting a free ride.

00:01:41.309 --> 00:01:45.191
Nina's never been to the
business class lounge before.

00:01:45.191 --> 00:01:47.411
What do you think, Nina? You
want to get something to eat?

00:01:47.411 --> 00:01:48.244
- Yeah.

00:01:48.244 --> 00:01:49.077
- [Evan] Get something to drink?

00:01:49.077 --> 00:01:49.910
- Yeah.

00:01:51.882 --> 00:01:53.631
- [Evan] I think Nina's really excited.

00:01:53.631 --> 00:01:54.464
- Bon appetit, guys.

00:01:54.464 --> 00:01:55.297
- [Evan] What did you get, Nina?

00:01:55.297 --> 00:01:59.380
- Salad, toast, and my
soup, and a glass of wine.

00:02:01.694 --> 00:02:03.286
- [Evan] Glass of wine, I got a beer,

00:02:03.286 --> 00:02:05.292
brand I've never heard
of, so I tried that.

00:02:05.292 --> 00:02:07.499
Mac and cheese, bread, salad.

00:02:07.499 --> 00:02:09.751
Nina's most excited
about the wine, I think.

00:02:09.751 --> 00:02:12.084
Free wine. You ready to eat?

00:02:13.502 --> 00:02:15.364
(chomping)

00:02:15.364 --> 00:02:18.014
We polished off a lot of
food there. Mostly Nina.

00:02:18.014 --> 00:02:19.708
- Three plates and a soup.

00:02:19.708 --> 00:02:23.048
- [Evan] Nina's nice and full
now. And she had her wine.

00:02:23.048 --> 00:02:24.362
Okay, so Nina, what are you

00:02:24.362 --> 00:02:27.860
most looking forward to on this trip?

00:02:27.860 --> 00:02:28.785
- Free food.

00:02:28.785 --> 00:02:29.642
- [Evan] Free food? Come on.

00:02:29.642 --> 00:02:33.539
- No, actually not free food.
Free calorie count food.

00:02:33.539 --> 00:02:35.872
- [Evan] You don't have to
go to Europe to do that.

00:02:35.872 --> 00:02:37.270
You can do that at home, you know.

00:02:37.270 --> 00:02:40.168
- Well, I'll also get to
see different countries.

00:02:40.168 --> 00:02:42.254
- [Evan] And spending, you know,

00:02:42.254 --> 00:02:45.159
an amazing week and a
half with your husband.

00:02:45.159 --> 00:02:45.992
- With me.

00:02:45.992 --> 00:02:46.831
- [Evan] With yourself?

00:02:46.831 --> 00:02:47.776
- Yeah.

00:02:47.776 --> 00:02:48.609
- [Evan] You get that every day.

00:02:48.609 --> 00:02:50.414
- Yeah, I get to see you every day.

00:02:50.414 --> 00:02:54.149
- [Evan] I'm looking
forward to seeing your face

00:02:54.149 --> 00:02:55.869
when we do the different sights.

00:02:55.869 --> 00:02:57.646
Because when you see new things...

00:02:57.646 --> 00:03:00.446
- What's that, what's that,
what's that, what's that.

00:03:00.446 --> 00:03:02.109
- [Evan] Yeah. You
freak out and your happy

00:03:02.109 --> 00:03:04.529
and excited and I love seeing that face.

00:03:04.529 --> 00:03:07.420
That's what I'm most excited for.

00:03:07.420 --> 00:03:09.989
We still have two and a
half hours before we leave

00:03:09.989 --> 00:03:11.656
so we've decided to,

00:03:13.228 --> 00:03:17.145
Nina made us hot chocolate
with Bailey's in it.

00:03:19.628 --> 00:03:21.286
Special Nina recipe.

00:03:21.286 --> 00:03:23.753
She's going to have some snacks.

00:03:23.753 --> 00:03:27.920
and we're going to watch some
Marvel Agents of S.H.I.E.L.D.

00:03:28.922 --> 00:03:31.089
Good way to pass the time.

00:03:32.894 --> 00:03:35.917
Nina and I ate way too
much, especially Nina.

00:03:35.917 --> 00:03:37.164
- Oh yeah, oh my gosh.

00:03:37.164 --> 00:03:39.277
- We're not used to eating this much food

00:03:39.277 --> 00:03:40.466
and so we're going to be on a cruise ship,

00:03:40.466 --> 00:03:42.384
where you can eat tons of food.

00:03:42.384 --> 00:03:43.460
- Yeah.

00:03:43.460 --> 00:03:46.487
- So we've got about an
hour before getting on,

00:03:46.487 --> 00:03:48.721
I was going to say getting
on the boat, on the plane?

00:03:48.721 --> 00:03:50.972
And we're going to try to walk off

00:03:50.972 --> 00:03:51.873
some of this food that we've had.

00:03:51.873 --> 00:03:53.297
- So we can eat again.

00:03:53.297 --> 00:03:54.560
- So that Nina can eat again on the plane.

00:03:54.560 --> 00:03:56.978
(laughing)

00:03:56.978 --> 00:03:59.149
- This is for you, Sean.

00:03:59.149 --> 00:03:59.982
- Shawn is our personal trainer.

00:03:59.982 --> 00:04:02.543
He keeps us on a very strict diet.

00:04:02.543 --> 00:04:06.710
And this is our 10 to 14
days to do whatever we want.

00:04:09.368 --> 00:04:10.201
- Calories.

00:04:10.201 --> 00:04:11.335
- Yeah.

00:04:11.335 --> 00:04:13.835
(light music)

00:04:16.859 --> 00:04:18.249
What happened, Nina?

00:04:18.249 --> 00:04:19.404
- Starbucks, so, Starbucks.

00:04:19.404 --> 00:04:20.237
- [Evan] There's a Starbucks behind you?

00:04:20.237 --> 00:04:22.800
I thought you were super full.

00:04:22.800 --> 00:04:23.722
- Pumpkin spice.

00:04:23.722 --> 00:04:24.555
- [Evan] Is it the first day

00:04:24.555 --> 00:04:27.556
of pumpkin spice latte, frappaccino?

00:04:27.556 --> 00:04:29.747
- Yeah, but I can't
have anything right now.

00:04:29.747 --> 00:04:30.718
- [Evan] Maybe after the walk?

00:04:30.718 --> 00:04:31.756
- Maybe after the walk.

00:04:31.756 --> 00:04:33.339
- [Evan] We'll see.

00:04:34.250 --> 00:04:35.974
What are you doing, Nina?

00:04:35.974 --> 00:04:37.360
- Too heavy.

00:04:37.360 --> 00:04:38.534
- [Evan] Too heavy on your back?

00:04:38.534 --> 00:04:39.367
- Yeah.

00:04:39.367 --> 00:04:40.200
- [Evan] Got to pack lighter.

00:04:40.200 --> 00:04:42.311
Everything I have for, how many days?

00:04:42.311 --> 00:04:46.478
12 days? 13 days? In this
backpack. Yeah. Travel light.

00:04:48.253 --> 00:04:50.753
(light music)

00:04:56.417 --> 00:04:59.179
Nina tried to put too
much stuff in her suitcase

00:04:59.179 --> 00:05:01.126
and she broke her zipper.

00:05:01.126 --> 00:05:04.176
- Ah, I thought I could fix it.

00:05:04.176 --> 00:05:07.132
- That's what happens when you
bring too much stuff, people.

00:05:07.132 --> 00:05:08.782
Pack light.

00:05:08.782 --> 00:05:11.282
(light music)

00:05:15.685 --> 00:05:17.025
You're not doing it.

00:05:17.025 --> 00:05:18.048
- I'm too full.

00:05:18.048 --> 00:05:19.106
- [Evan] Too full?

00:05:19.106 --> 00:05:19.939
- Yeah.

00:05:19.939 --> 00:05:20.772
- [Evan] That walk didn't help?

00:05:20.772 --> 00:05:24.013
That crazy work out and fixing your bag?

00:05:24.013 --> 00:05:24.846
- No.

00:05:24.846 --> 00:05:27.432
- [Evan] No? Alright. No
pumpkin spice frappuccino.

00:05:27.432 --> 00:05:31.900
- I don't know. Maybe I have
to walk around two more times.

00:05:31.900 --> 00:05:34.221
- [Evan] There it is,
Nina. Starbucks. Hello.

00:05:34.221 --> 00:05:36.161
We haven't convinced her
yet. Let's see what happens.

00:05:36.161 --> 00:05:38.661
(light music)

00:05:42.959 --> 00:05:45.376
What's that over there, Nina?

00:05:46.460 --> 00:05:48.485
Oh, we're not going?

00:05:48.485 --> 00:05:51.402
Nina's decided officially too full.

00:05:52.365 --> 00:05:54.400
Can't handle Starbucks.

00:05:54.400 --> 00:05:57.817
We'll look for a pumpkin spice in London.

00:05:58.684 --> 00:06:00.424
Nina's crashing out.

00:06:00.424 --> 00:06:01.257
- Tired.

00:06:01.257 --> 00:06:02.848
- [Evan] She's tired.
Let's get her on the plane.

00:06:02.848 --> 00:06:06.598
Get her sleeping, and
arrive in London. Yeah.

00:06:09.319 --> 00:06:11.524
Alright, we had a delay.

00:06:11.524 --> 00:06:12.357
- Yeah.

00:06:12.357 --> 00:06:13.272
Nina's not happy about this delay.

00:06:13.272 --> 00:06:14.105
- I'm so tired.

00:06:14.105 --> 00:06:15.577
- Well welcome to my life,

00:06:15.577 --> 00:06:17.768
like every trip I go on is a delay.

00:06:17.768 --> 00:06:20.076
It's why I hate traveling.

00:06:20.076 --> 00:06:24.866
But we made it on, Nina's
excited, get to our seats,

00:06:24.866 --> 00:06:29.033
get to sleep, she's going
to eat some more guaranteed.

00:06:30.902 --> 00:06:32.485
This is me, four D.

00:06:34.904 --> 00:06:36.654
There's Nina, four G.

00:06:37.833 --> 00:06:38.833
- It's cool.

00:06:41.214 --> 00:06:42.671
- [Evan] What's cool?

00:06:42.671 --> 00:06:44.824
- Like here, room to put my feet up.

00:06:44.824 --> 00:06:47.358
- [Evan] You could sleep, you
could lay down properly, huh?

00:06:47.358 --> 00:06:48.191
- Yeah.

00:06:48.191 --> 00:06:50.146
- [Evan] Alright, she's excited.

00:06:50.146 --> 00:06:53.327
Here, you got headphones.
We've got some headphones.

00:06:53.327 --> 00:06:57.543
We've got some water, even
here we got some toiletries.

00:06:57.543 --> 00:06:58.376
What do you have.

00:06:58.376 --> 00:06:59.209
- We have socks.

00:06:59.209 --> 00:07:03.721
- [Evan] Okay, good, so you
don't get smelly feet. Okay.

00:07:03.721 --> 00:07:06.054
And then, what else you got?

00:07:07.124 --> 00:07:10.187
Eye mask. How Cool. And then?

00:07:10.187 --> 00:07:12.437
- And then cleansing cloth.

00:07:14.106 --> 00:07:15.507
- [Evan] Cleansing cloth, okay.

00:07:15.507 --> 00:07:16.497
- And lip balm.

00:07:16.497 --> 00:07:17.472
- [Evan] Exciting for you.

00:07:17.472 --> 00:07:18.598
- And lotion

00:07:18.598 --> 00:07:22.187
- [Evan] Lotion. All right. Toothbrush.

00:07:22.187 --> 00:07:23.020
- That's important.

00:07:23.020 --> 00:07:25.603
(light music)

00:07:29.318 --> 00:07:32.855
- [Evan] The menu came.
See what we're eating.

00:07:32.855 --> 00:07:34.522
Late evening supper.

00:07:35.586 --> 00:07:38.550
Do I want to be woken up for breakfast?

00:07:38.550 --> 00:07:39.383
Probably.

00:07:39.383 --> 00:07:42.527
My favorite part is I get
to watch foreign movies,

00:07:42.527 --> 00:07:44.910
cause it's always a good
selection on the plane.

00:07:44.910 --> 00:07:46.598
So I watch the Chinese ones with Nina

00:07:46.598 --> 00:07:48.654
so there's some Korean action movies

00:07:48.654 --> 00:07:50.627
that I'm looking forward to watching.

00:07:50.627 --> 00:07:52.123
I'm going to start with this one.

00:07:52.123 --> 00:07:54.123
Confidential Assignment.

00:07:55.333 --> 00:07:59.272
Nina, on the other hand,
wants to watch cartoons.

00:07:59.272 --> 00:08:00.580
She's going to watch a cartoon

00:08:00.580 --> 00:08:03.080
with a purple hippo and a cat.

00:08:03.925 --> 00:08:06.722
She's just a kid at heart.
That's partly why we love her.

00:08:06.722 --> 00:08:09.026
Also noise canceling headphones,

00:08:09.026 --> 00:08:11.830
so Nina's trying to tell me something.

00:08:11.830 --> 00:08:14.913
Nina, what are you trying to tell me.

00:08:15.873 --> 00:08:20.040
I have no idea what she's
saying. Noise canceling.

00:08:23.022 --> 00:08:27.105
Here's dinner. I got some
steak, potatoes, bread,

00:08:28.138 --> 00:08:29.777
cheese,

00:08:29.777 --> 00:08:30.610
fruit,

00:08:31.693 --> 00:08:32.526
salad,

00:08:33.408 --> 00:08:34.908
